{"id":"word:hebrew:H2778","type":"word","title":"חָרַף","subtitle":"H2778 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to pull off , i.e. (by implication) to expose (as by stripping); specifically, to betroth (as if a surrender); figuratively, to carp at , i.e. defame ; to spend the winter","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to חָרַף (H2778) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 41 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"חָרַף (châraph) means to pull off , i.e. (by implication) to expose (as by stripping); specifically, to betroth (as if a surrender); figuratively, to carp at , i.e. defame ; to spend the winter First listed occurrence: 1Chr 20 7."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"חָרַף","transliteration":"châraph","pronunciation":"khaw-raf'","strong":"H2778","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2778","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["חֵרֵ֣ף","וַ/יְחָרֵ֖ף","חֵרֵ֔ף","לְ/חָרֵף֙","לְ/חָרֵ֖ף"],"morphs":[["HVpp3ms",7],["HR/Vpc",6],["HVpp2ms",5],["HVpp3cp",4],["HVpp3cp/Sp1cs",3],["HC/Vpw3ms",2],["HVqrmsc/Sp1cs",2],["HVpp1cs",1],["HR/Vpc/Sp3mp",1],["HVqi3fs",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"to pull off , i.e. (by implication) to expose (as by stripping); specifically, to betroth (as if a surrender); figuratively, to carp at , i.e. defame ; to spend the winter","usage":"betroth, blaspheme, defy, jeopard, rail, reproach, upbraid.","full":"H2778. charaph . I. [ חָרַף ] verb reproach (Late Hebrew Pi`el id. ; Aramaic חֲרַף id. , sharpen , sharp, keen, acute ); — Qal Imperfect מִיָּמָ֑י לְבָבִי לֹאיֶֿחֱרַף Job 27:6 ; Participle suffix חֹרְפִי Psa 119:42 ; Prov 27:11 ; חוֺרְפֶיךָ Psa 69:10 . Piel. Perfect חֵרֵף Judg 5:18 6 t.; חֵרַפְתָּ Isa 37:23 4 t. etc. + 10 t. perfect; Imperfect יְחָרֵף 2Sam 21:21 ; 1Chr 20:7 ; יְחָ֫רֶף Psa 74:10 2 t. suffix; Infinitive לְחָרֵף Isa 37:4-5 t.; בְּחָֽרְפָם 2Sam 23:9 (but see below); Participle מְחָרֵף Psa 44:17 ; &#8212; reproach , — properly say sharp things against , — taunt , with accusative Judg 8:15 ; 1Sam 17:10 , 25 , 26 , 36 , 45 ; 2Sam 21:21 1Chr 20:7 ; God, by injustice to the poor Prov 14:31 ; 17:5 ; Yahweh, by idolatry Isa 65:7 ; Yahweh as the God of Israel 2Kin 19:4 , 16 , 22 , 23 = Isa 37:4 ; 37:17 ; 37:23 ; 37:24 2Chr 32:17 (with לְ ); with בְּ , Philistines 2Sam 23:9 ᵑ0 (but read דַּמִּים בְּפַס at Pas-dammîm , proper name, of a location, as 1Chr 11:12 We Dr); reproach , Neh 6:13 + Neh 42:11; Neh 44:17; Neh 55:13; Neh 57:4; Neh 74:10; Neh 74:18; Neh 79:12; Neh 89:52 (twice in verse); Neh 102:9; Zeph 2:8 , 10 ; in poetry and figurative, despise, scorn , ׳ח למוּת נפשׁ Judg 5:18 . III. [ חָרַף ] verb denominative remain in harvest-time (so Arabic ; English to winter ) — only Qal Imperfect 3feminine singular תֶּחֱרָ֑ף עָלָיו הָאָרֶץ כָּלבֶּֿהֱמַת Isa 18:6 all the beasts of the earth shall spend the harvest-time upon it . IV. [ חָרַף ] verb acquire (compare Arabic turn a thing from its proper way or manner , but also gain, acquire [subsistence] for one's family) — only Niph`al Participle f. לְאִישׁ נֶחֱרֶפֶת שִׁפְחָה a maidservant acquired for a man (namely as his concubine) Lev 19:26 (H; compare Late Hebrew חֲרוּפָה of woman designated for a man).","rootNote":"a primitive root; also denominative (from 2779 )","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 20 7","keyReferences":["1Chr 20 7","1Sam 17 10","1Sam 17 25","1Sam 17 26","1Sam 17 36","1Sam 17 45","2Chr 32 17","2Kgs 19 4"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":41,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 20 7","book":"1Chr","chapter":20,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יְחָרֵ֖ף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpw3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 17 10","book":"1Sam","chapter":17,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חֵרַ֛פְתִּי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVpp1cs"},{"reference":"1Sam 17 25","book":"1Sam","chapter":17,"verse":25,"englishText